framework PurposeBusRcHardening:
  requires problem and decision
  requires premise and evidence
  warns pending

domain PurposeBus:
  description "Local-first coordination queue for human and AI agent instances"

problem P1:
  |
    What bounded implementation and evidence are required to move the
    owner-accepted read-only MCP beta to V0_9_RC_READY without starting the
    later Codex-controller, Plugin 1.0 packaging, installation, or publication
    work?

premise PR1:
  |
    The user authorized proceeding with T_RC_HARDENING after accepting the
    exact beta candidate, but did not authorize commit, push, profile mutation,
    public marketplace submission, release, deployment, Connector use, or
    agent launch.

premise PR2:
  |
    T_RC_HARDENING requires public JSON, CLI, MCP adapter, and current Skill-only
    Plugin compatibility to be frozen and requires upgrade, rollback, bounded
    load, corruption, provenance, environment, permission, documentation, and
    release-automation evidence on immutable local candidates.

premise PR3:
  |
    T_V1_PLUGIN_PACKAGE remains downstream of owner acceptance of the RC, so
    this task must not turn the current Skill-only Plugin into the later 1.0
    package or add the read-only MCP server to the Plugin manifest.

evidence EV1:
  |
    The active roadmap reports V0_5_BETA_ACCEPTED as reached and accepted,
    records T_BETA_BUILD done, and recommends T_RC_HARDENING next.

evidence EV2:
  |
    Local HEAD and the independently read GitHub feature/local-mvp ref both
    equal 2a2b3a68c8f44a4107268e4fd51949106a37d486; the accepted beta is
    uncommitted workspace content on that base.

evidence EV3:
  |
    The accepted beta has core 0.2.0a1, MCP adapter 0.1.0a0, controller policy
    skeleton 0.0.0a0, Plugin 0.2.0 plus a Codex cachebuster, public response
    schemas purposebus.*.v2, error schema purposebus.error.v1, and state schema
    version 1.

evidence EV4:
  |
    Existing tests already cover deterministic public projections, bounded
    inputs, private state permissions, concurrency, corrupt and unknown state,
    Plugin package structure, MCP fail-closed behavior, and isolated wheel
    contents, but the repository has no one-command immutable RC manifest and
    no artifact-bound upgrade and rollback verification.

evidence EV5:
  |
    Official OpenAI Plugin documentation says local and repository marketplaces
    are separate authoring and testing sources from public publication, and a
    complete skills-only Plugin test uses a local install, a new conversation,
    and direct, indirect, follow-up, negative, and unsupported cases.

premise IN1:
  |
    Inference: because the roadmap milestone name is not the installed package
    version and the accepted beta deliberately uses independently versioned
    packages, changing every package to 0.9.0 merely to match V0_9_RC_READY
    would introduce an unsupported compatibility decision rather than harden
    the accepted candidate.

premise ALT1:
  |
    Alternative: immediately install into the active Codex profile and exercise
    a live conversation. This can test pickup behavior, but it exceeds the
    current profile-mutation boundary and is not necessary for artifact-local
    RC hardening.

premise ALT2:
  |
    Alternative: add documentation only. This cannot establish upgrade,
    rollback, load, corruption, provenance, or permission behavior and does not
    satisfy the implementation contract.

premise ALT3:
  |
    Alternative: first add an executable clean-room RC verifier and a frozen
    machine-readable compatibility manifest, run it on an immutable local
    source snapshot, and record only the actually observed environment and
    known limitations. This exercises the required mechanisms without profile
    or external mutation.

pending PD1:
  |
    Active-profile fresh-conversation behavior, other Linux distributions,
    other Codex versions, public Plugin Directory review, signing identity, and
    publication destinations remain unverified and cannot be claimed by local
    clean-room evidence.

decision D1 based_on P1, PR1, PR2, PR3, EV1, EV2, EV3, EV4, EV5, IN1, ALT1, ALT2, ALT3, PD1:
  |
    Start T_RC_HARDENING on the existing feature/local-mvp WIP. Preserve the
    accepted package and public-schema versions. Add an accepted compatibility
    and provenance ADR, a machine-readable RC contract, and repository-owned
    automation that creates a source snapshot and wheels, binds their digests,
    installs only into temporary environments, verifies beta-to-candidate
    upgrade and rollback, reopens supported state across both versions, checks
    corrupt-state fail-closed behavior, runs bounded load and permission tests,
    validates Plugin and MCP contracts, and emits a local evidence manifest.
    Run the existing full suites and the new verifier. Record current WSL/Linux,
    Python, and Codex versions as observed support evidence, retain all other
    environments as limitations, and stop at V0_9_RC_READY for separate owner
    acceptance. Do not install into an active profile, commit, push, publish,
    release, deploy, add controller behavior, add MCP to the Plugin, use a
    Connector, or launch agents.

query Q1:
  .document.steps[].statement | select(.role == "decision" and len(.based_on) > 0)
